.TH CIRCQ_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
circq_send_zc \- send a message to the queue (blocking)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t circq_send_zc(circular_queue *cq, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Blocks until space is available in the queue, then transfers ownership of
the message data to the queue. The msg->data pointer is set to NULL on
success (zero-copy semantics).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq   Circular queue to send to
msg  Message to send (data ownership transfers on success)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - Message sent successfully
ccol_invalid_args  - cq or msg is NULL, or msg validation fails
ccol_not_permitted - Sending has been disabled
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Blocks indefinitely until space is available or sending is disabled
After waking from blocking, rechecks if sending is still enabled
On failure, caller retains ownership of msg->data
msg->data == NULL with msg->size == 0 is valid (sentinel message)
msg->data == NULL with msg->size > 0 is invalid
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR circq_try_send_zc (3),
.BR circq_timed_send_zc (3),
.BR circq_recv_zc (3)
